@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Application Components — Modular Monolith
package "Angular SPA" {
  [AuthService / Guards / DashboardLayout] as authui
  [Customer Accounts\n(dashboard + shared account-selector)] as acctui
  [Customer Transactions] as txui
  [Customer Disputes] as dui
  [Agent Workspace] as aui
}
package "Spring Boot" {
  [Auth / Security] as sec
  [Spring Session JDBC] as sessions
  [Auth Accounts / Activity] as authstore
  [Account (GET /accounts, V5)] as acct
  [Transaction (GET /transactions, V6)] as trans
  [Dispute API / Application] as app
  [Dispute Domain] as domain
  [Dispute Audit submodule] as audit
  [Idempotency] as idem
  [Technical Infrastructure] as infra
}
database PostgreSQL
authui --> sec
acctui --> acct
txui --> acctui : shared account API client (GET /accounts)
txui --> trans
trans --> acct : AccountFixturePort (fixture only)
dui --> app
aui --> app
app --> sec : authenticated principal
app --> trans : owned transaction lookup / lock interface
app --> domain
app --> audit : synchronous append interface
app --> idem
sec --> sessions : server-side sessions
sessions --> PostgreSQL : shared session state
sec --> authstore : narrow account/activity interfaces
authstore --> PostgreSQL : app_users / version / guarded activity
acct --> PostgreSQL
trans --> PostgreSQL
app --> PostgreSQL
audit --> PostgreSQL
idem --> PostgreSQL
note bottom
One Spring Boot deployment; no cross-module repository access.
account module owns accounts table (V5); transaction module owns bank_transactions (V6).
transaction fixture accesses account IDs through narrow public AccountFixturePort only.
Shared account-selector is a presentational Angular component in shared/components;
account data fetching stays in the accounts feature service.
Dispute, audit and idempotency writes share one PostgreSQL transaction.
Infrastructure: envelopes, correlation IDs, validation and exception mapping.
No microservices or API Gateway in MVP.
Auth/session infrastructure implemented; business modules remain future scope.
end note
@enduml
